<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DocBook XML V4.5//EN"
 "/usr/share/sgml/docbook/xml-dtd-4.5/docbookx.dtd">
<article id="kcm_zenbook_platform">
<title>ZenBook Platform — System Settings</title>
<articleinfo>
 <authorgroup>
  <author><firstname>zenbook_scripts</firstname></author>
 </authorgroup>
</articleinfo>

<sect1 id="overview">
<title>Overview</title>
<para>
The <application>ZenBook Platform</application> module configures ASUS ZenBook Duo
platform tools shipped with <application>zenbook-scripts</application>: keyboard
backlight and hotkeys, dual-eDP dock, ScreenPad backlight, sleep/resume session
policy, scheduled profiles, and touchpad live-filter knobs.
</para>
<para>
Most settings are stored under
<filename>~/.config/zenbook-scripts/</filename> and
<filename>/etc/zenbook-scripts/</filename>. OpenRC services are installed by
<command>configure.py</command> on Gentoo.
</para>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="overview-tab">
<title>Overview tab</title>
<para>
Shows output of <command>platform-probe</command> (machine detection, fan backends,
platform_profile, touchpad nodes). Loaded automatically when the module opens.
Use <guilabel>Refresh</guilabel> after plugging the keyboard dock or resuming from sleep.
</para>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="displays-tab">
<title>Displays tab</title>
<para>
Duo dock and ScreenPad status are populated when the module opens. Use
<guilabel>Refresh</guilabel> only if hardware changed while System Settings stayed open.
</para>
<sect2 id="duo-dock">
<title>Duo dock (UX8406 / UX581)</title>
<para>
Lower eDP panel management via <command>platform-duo-dock</command>. Status is loaded
when the module opens.
</para>
<itemizedlist>
 <listitem><para><guilabel>Docked</guilabel> — enable lower panel in stacked layout.</para></listitem>
 <listitem><para><guilabel>Undocked</guilabel> — disable lower panel.</para></listitem>
 <listitem><para><guilabel>Screen swap</guilabel> — toggle primary between upper/lower via <command>platform-screen-swap</command>.</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</sect2>
<sect2 id="screenpad">
<title>ScreenPad (UX5400 and similar)</title>
<para>
Secondary panel backlight through <command>screenpad</command> (asus_screenpad sysfs).
Not the same as Duo eDP-2.
</para>
<itemizedlist>
 <listitem><para><guilabel>On</guilabel> / <guilabel>Off</guilabel> — power and brightness.</para></listitem>
 <listitem><para><guilabel>Sync to main</guilabel> — mirror main panel brightness percentage once.</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</sect2>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="sleep-resume">
<title>Sleep / Resume tab</title>
<para>
Per-user session policy in <filename>~/.config/zenbook-scripts/session.json</filename>
(managed by <command>platform-session</command>).
</para>
<variablelist>
 <varlistentry>
  <term>Restore presentation after plasmashell replace</term>
  <listitem><para>Re-applies PowerDevil presentation mode after <command>plasmashell --replace</command> (that inhibit is owned by plasmashell and is lost on replace).</para></listitem>
 </varlistentry>
 <varlistentry>
  <term>Watch QSG render threads</term>
  <listitem><para>After resume, count plasmashell threads named QSGRenderThread / Mesa (gdrv, traceq). Useful on Plasma 6.6 Wayland when resume leaks render threads (common on dual-eDP Duo). Off by default.</para></listitem>
 </varlistentry>
 <varlistentry>
  <term>Auto plasmashell --replace</term>
  <listitem><para>When watch is on and thread count exceeds the threshold, run <command>plasmashell --replace</command> (does not kill apps; kwin_wayland keeps windows).</para></listitem>
 </varlistentry>
 <varlistentry>
  <term>QSG thread threshold</term>
  <listitem><para>Total QSG/Mesa-related threads across plasmashell PIDs before auto-replace. Healthy: under ~16; leaked resume on Duo often exceeds 32. Range 1–256; default 32. Check manually: <command>platform-session plasmashell check</command>.</para></listitem>
 </varlistentry>
</variablelist>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="profiles-tab">
<title>Profiles tab</title>
<para>
Edits <filename>~/.config/zenbook-scripts/profiles.json</filename> (day/night schedules,
fan curves, keyboard backlight levels). <guilabel>Apply</guilabel> writes JSON;
<command>platform-profiles</command> evaluates schedules via cron.
</para>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="touchpad-tab">
<title>Touchpad tab</title>
<para>
Knobs for the <emphasis>live filter</emphasis> (<command>platform-touchpad run</command>).
Settings are saved to
<filename>~/.config/zenbook-scripts/touchpad.json</filename> when present, else
<filename>/etc/zenbook-scripts/touchpad.json</filename>.
</para>
<important>
<para>
<emphasis>Soft accel</emphasis> and palm filters only apply when the live filter is
running (<guilabel>Start live filter</guilabel> or OpenRC
<literal>zenbook-platform-touchpad</literal>). Raw libinput in Plasma is unchanged.
After changing knobs, click <guilabel>Apply</guilabel> — the module restarts the live
filter if it was already running.
</para>
</important>
<variablelist>
 <varlistentry>
  <term>Filter profile</term>
  <listitem>
   <para><literal>default</literal> — static outlier_reject + exec_delay chain.</para>
   <para><literal>adaptive</literal> — adaptive_matrix learns per-axis noise; small isolated glitches are attenuated (clamped), not dropped. Fast swipes pass through. State under <filename>~/.config/zenbook-scripts/adaptive-touchpad/</filename>.</para>
  </listitem>
 </varlistentry>
 <varlistentry>
  <term>Soft accel</term>
  <listitem><para>Scales ABS motion on the uinput device (DE AccelSpeed bypass). Try 160–200% (gain 1.6–2.0). Nonlinear mode available in the full tuner.</para></listitem>
 </varlistentry>
 <varlistentry>
  <term>Live status</term>
  <listitem><para>Output of <command>platform-touchpad status</command> — loaded when the module opens. Shows config path, daemon PID, per-pad filter chain.</para></listitem>
 </varlistentry>
</variablelist>
<para>
USB and Bluetooth transport settings are stored under nested
<literal>transports.usb</literal> / <literal>transports.bluetooth</literal> on the logical
device name. Stale flat composite keys are removed on save.
</para>
<para>
<guilabel>Open full tuner…</guilabel> launches <application>platform-touchpad-gui</application>
(calibrate wizard, monitor, adaptive stats).
</para>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="cli">
<title>Command-line reference</title>
<simplelist type="vert">
 <member><command>platform-probe</command></member>
 <member><command>platform-duo-dock status|docked|undocked</command></member>
 <member><command>platform-screen-swap toggle</command></member>
 <member><command>screenpad status|on|off|sync</command></member>
 <member><command>platform-touchpad status|run|stop</command></member>
 <member><command>platform-touchpad-kcm export|import</command></member>
 <member><command>platform-touchpad-gui</command></member>
 <member><command>platform-session plasmashell check</command></member>
 <member><command>platform-profiles status|set</command></member>
 <member><command>kb-brightness</command> / <command>kb-brightness-hotkeys</command></member>
</simplelist>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="config-files">
<title>Configuration files</title>
<itemizedlist>
 <listitem><para><filename>~/.config/zenbook-scripts/session.json</filename></para></listitem>
 <listitem><para><filename>~/.config/zenbook-scripts/profiles.json</filename></para></listitem>
 <listitem><para><filename>~/.config/zenbook-scripts/touchpad.json</filename></para></listitem>
 <listitem><para><filename>~/.config/zenbook-scripts/adaptive-touchpad/*.json</filename></para></listitem>
 <listitem><para><filename>/etc/zenbook-scripts/</filename> (system defaults)</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="services">
<title>OpenRC services</title>
<simplelist type="vert">
 <member><literal>zenbook-kb-hotkeys</literal></member>
 <member><literal>zenbook-kb-lid</literal></member>
 <member><literal>zenbook-platform-touchpad</literal></member>
 <member><literal>zenbook-screenpad</literal></member>
</simplelist>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="troubleshooting">
<title>Troubleshooting</title>
<sect2 id="ts-live-status">
<title>Live status empty</title>
<para>
Rebuild and install the KCM plugin, restart System Settings. Run
<command>platform-touchpad status</command> in a terminal to verify CLI output.
</para>
</sect2>
<sect2 id="ts-soft-accel">
<title>Soft accel does nothing</title>
<para>
Start the live filter, enable Soft accel, Apply, and confirm status counters increase.
Ensure the filtered uinput pad is the one in use.
</para>
</sect2>
<sect2 id="ts-adaptive">
<title>Adaptive sticky or jumpy</title>
<para>
Reset learned state: remove files under
<filename>~/.config/zenbook-scripts/adaptive-touchpad/</filename> and restart the live filter.
Current builds attenuate glitches instead of dropping frames.
</para>
</sect2>
<sect2 id="ts-help">
<title>Help: Documentation not Found</title>
<para>
Install handbook: <command>cd plasma/kcm &amp;&amp; sudo env PREFIX=/usr ./build.sh --system</command>.
Expected path: <filename>/usr/share/doc/HTML/en/kcm_zenbook_platform/index.html</filename>.
</para>
</sect2>
</sect1>

